{"name":"Yù Shí Bái White","hex":"#c0e2e1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yu Shi","blocks":[{"text":"Yu Shi is a Chinese spirit or god of rain, also known as or conflated with Red Pine, among other names. Translations of Yu Shi into English include \"Lord of Rain\" and \"Leader of Rain\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yu_Shi"},{"title":"Henan","blocks":[{"text":"Henan is a province in Central China. Henan is China's third-most populous province and the most populous among inland provinces, with a population of over 99 million as of 2020. The area around Henan was historically known as the Central Plains (Zhongyuan) and is considered the core region of Chinese cultural history.Four of the historical capitals of China, Luoyang, Anyang, Kaifeng and Zhengzhou, are in Henan. People from Henan sometimes underwent discrimination within China."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Shang_Inscribed_Ox_Scapula_%28for_divination%29.jpg/330px-Shang_Inscribed_Ox_Scapula_%28for_divination%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henan"},{"title":"Bai (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Bái is the pinyin of the surname 白, meaning the colour white."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b8/%E7%99%BD-order.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bai_(surname)"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/%E9%BE%99%E9%97%A8%E7%9F%B3%E7%AA%9F%E4%B8%BB%E7%AA%9F_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg/500px-%E9%BE%99%E9%97%A8%E7%9F%B3%E7%AA%9F%E4%B8%BB%E7%AA%9F_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/%E9%BE%99%E9%97%A8%E7%9F%B3%E7%AA%9F%E4%B8%BB%E7%AA%9F_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg/1280px-%E9%BE%99%E9%97%A8%E7%9F%B3%E7%AA%9F%E4%B8%BB%E7%AA%9F_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/%E9%BE%99%E9%97%A8%E7%9F%B3%E7%AA%9F%E4%B8%BB%E7%AA%9F_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg/500px-%E9%BE%99%E9%97%A8%E7%9F%B3%E7%AA%9F%E4%B8%BB%E7%AA%9F_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%E9%BE%99%E9%97%A8%E7%9F%B3%E7%AA%9F%E4%B8%BB%E7%AA%9F_-_panoramio_(1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/20250608_Gaocheng_Observatory_02.jpg/500px-20250608_Gaocheng_Observatory_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia